[C1] PASS w2 (I + w2 dt M)^-1 (dt L) = (I + w2 dt M)^-1 (w2 dt L): weighting the solved du is the same as weighting the right-hand side, once dt_corr carries w2: max relative difference 4.5e-16
[C2] PASS dt_corr / dt per stage: rk3 and rk3s4 are weighted by wght2, rk1 and rk2 use the full dt: rk1 1; rk2 1, 1; rk3 1, 0.25, 0.6667; rk3s4 0.5, 0.5, 0.1667, 0.5
[C3] PASS on a stiff mode the weighted correction damps rk3 to 1/12 per step and rk3s4 to 0; with the full dt they damp to 1/3 and 17/48: R(z = 1e8): rk3 weighted 0.083333, full dt 0.333333; rk3s4 weighted 0.000000, full dt 0.354167
[C4] PASS every integrator with the correction keeps |R(z)| <= 1 for z in [1e-3, 1e8]; a fully implicit decay converges at first order (the correction is a linearised backward Euler): max |R| = 0.9990; rk3 errors at 40, 80, 160 steps 8.81e-03, 4.41e-03, 2.21e-03, fitted order 1.00
[C5] PASS as Z -> oo the stage takes w0 Y^n + (w1 - 1) Y weighted and w0 Y^n + (w1 - w2) Y with the full dt; the rk3 stages then give 1/12 and 1/3, the rk3s4 stages 0 and 17/48, exactly: rk3 weighted 0, 3/4, 1/12; rk3 full dt 0, 3/4, 1/3; rk3s4 weighted 0, 0, 2/3, 0; rk3s4 full dt 1/2, 1/4, 17/24, 17/48
